lusombra_0="Lusombra"
lusombra_1="Lucilla was a prominent student at the Temple of Ayeela, studying to become a Priestess of Light. She excelled in magical prowess and determination, and with her strong faith she would become instrumental to the successful cleansing of the Temple. It ultimately also led her into darkness."
lusombra_2="During the Fall, Lucilla managed to slip away and stay hidden, surviving on her own in the dark Temple halls. She carefully wandered the halls, avoiding her now corrupted friends, mentors, and former protectors. Ultimately, she came upon the Knights Templar who had arrived to purge the Temple, and they swore to protect her until order was restored. Little did they know, the roles would soon be reversed."
lusombra_3="In a desperate moment, as the Knights Templar were overwhelmed by the hordes of undead, they focused their holy magic and faith unto Lucilla, as she walked untouched through the darkness, brimming with holy light. In a final encounter with the corrupted High Priest Medella, Lucilla would become the Avatar of Ayeela, and slay her former mentor, freeing the Temple of the corruption upon it."
lusombra_4="Lucilla ended up joining the Templars, becoming a great leader and inspiration for all. Here she discovered that not only was she exceedingly proficient in the ways of Holy magic, but she was also able to manipulate Shadow magic to strengthen it. She from then on took on the name Lusombra - Light in Shadow. ''In total darkness, the light shines stronger.''"
templar_0="Knights Templar"
templar_1="The Knights Templar were divided into many orders, most of which no longer exist today due to internal fighting and corruption. However, Knights from the Order of Light were those who ultimately cleansed The Fallen Temple, and their ways are still practiced to this day."
templar_2="A particularly notable order that no longer exists is the Order of Death. The Knight Templars of this order called themselves Death Knights, and practised Shadow magic and various forms of Necromancy. They were exiled after multiple tragic events involving Shadow  magic, and would abandon all their Knightly ways, in favor of continuing the practices of Shadow magic in secrecy."
templar_3="Today, only a singular great Order of Templars remain, which is the result of all the remaining loyal Orders merging. Three schools of Magic are practiced freely in any combination, along with swordsmanship and heavy armor proficiency. Those schools of magic are Fire, Lightning, and, of course, Holy. "
actelves_0="The Elven War"
actelves_1="The Elven War is regarded as the most terrible and most important historical event in recent times. It was a terrible war of immense destruction and loss of life, but it ultimately also led to peace, unity, and an everlasting alliance between adversaries."
actelves_2="After the war was over, it was discovered that both Humans and Elves had been influenced by an unknown actor, pulling strings from the shadows. They had been driven towards conflict with one another to remain weakened and burdened by war. While the Human invasion of the Elven Realms were in many ways successful, all land seized was immediately returned upon the discovery of the true enemy."
actelves_3="Demons. The fierce beasts from the mystical plane of fire, masters of deception and terror. They had pushed Humans and Elves on a collision course for decades. With the true enemy revealed, Humans immediately began helping the Elves restore their lands, treaties were signed, and an alliance was forged. News of the hidden threat spread, and over the course of a generation, several other races lended their aid and strength to rebuild, and amass a great unified army. This army would march upon the Gates of Hell, entering The Last War of our time."
heroeselves_0="Notable Heroes of The War"
heroeselves_1="The War both created and destroyed great champions and heroes on both sides. Notably, Commander Marruu of the humans earned many accolades for her distinguished service, and several of her subordinates, including Lieutenant Fredricks, Sergeant Jorgen, and Private Jim would all become honored heroes of Humanity."
heroeselves_2="Among the Elves, the losses were much greater, and most of their notable champions and leaders fell in combat. Cael’is, Feren’el, and Oakstorm all received posthumous accolades from the Humans in recognition of their sacrifice for their people, as part of Humans making amends. Stamm the Unbreakable was welcomed and honored by Elves and Humans alike when he regrew, now free of the influence of Demons."
heroeselves_3="In a joint effort between Elves and Humans, a monument was later constructed in memory of those who fell. The memories of the fallen heroes would later also be included in the simulations of the Chronicon, though it does simulate from the perspective of the human aggressors, which has led to some debate. Many descendants of leaders and heroes of both sides of the Elven War would later meet in battle again, however this time they’d be fighting alongside one another, against a common foe."
warden_0="The Wardens"
warden_1="As part of the peace agreement between Humans and Elves, Humans were taught how to tend to and safeguard their own forests. Previously, Humans had merely cut them down for wood and to make room for farmland. But the Elves taught them how to maintain them for an unlimited supply of wood without the need of destroying them entirely."
warden_2="However the forests also had to be protected from evil and wrongdoing, be it from creatures or other Humans who lived outside the boundaries of law. Not only that, but the people who worked in the forests also needed protection and safety. Thus came the Wardens."
warden_3="The Wardens were initially a mix of Elves and Humans, as the Elven Rangers and Druids were teaching their Human allies their ways. The Wardens quickly became experts in archery and several schools of magic that aligned with nature, such as Lightning, Frost, and Poison."
warden_4="The Wardens also became master beast tamers, and would often be accompanied by beasts, fae, and other magical creatures. Today, the Wardens are still a mix of Humans and Elves, but in a different sense, as all Wardens today are both Elf and Man. A symbol of the union and everlasting peace of two species, the Wardens are highly regarded among both peoples."
actcastle_0="King Weyrick"
actcastle_1="We still don’t know exactly what illness befell King Weyrick, or if it even was an illness and not a curse of some kind. We do know it was impossible to cure, and drove a great Doctor to desperation and, eventually, complete madness."
actcastle_2="In life, Weyrick was a great king, and held the largest castle ever built. This also meant holding a large staff, and accommodations and facilities for them. The castle had endless corridors of seemingly identical rooms, common rooms, storages, kitchens, great gardens, and even its own catacombs."
actcastle_3="Ultimately, the King passed from his mysterious illness, but it didn’t take long for him to return to his throne. In death, he remained, as madness took hold. It wasn’t until a band of adventurers delved deep into the now decrepit and overrun Castle Clairebourg that he was finally slain, and could rest."
peoplecastle_0="Victims of Madness"
peoplecastle_1="A servant named Charles would be the one referred to as Patient Zero. He endured some of the most torturous experimentation of the Doctor, and his twisted form long stalked the dark halls of Castle Clairebourg. He would eventually be freed from his madness by adventurers, and his spirit soon joined his beloved, who had pleaded for their help."
peoplecastle_2="Madam Prides oversaw the servant quarters at Castle Clairebourg. A respected, hard-working and kind woman, she kept everyone fed and everything clean. But some say she secretly fed the massive spiders in the basement with unruly servants."
peoplecastle_3="Khelagar was the assistant to the Doctor, and was both a victim and perpetrator of violence and experimentation. He himself was terribly misshapen, and experimented just as much on himself as his victims. He came to be responsible for raising the dead in the Catacombs, before he was eventually slain by adventurers."
warlock_0="The Warlocks"
warlock_1="The Warlocks, formerly known as the Death Knights of the Templar Order of Death, were by this point entirely shunned and exiled. Far too many fell to the corruption of Shadow magics, and far too many innocent lives were lost in their wake. Today, however, the Warlocks still exist and operate outside the Order, but are no longer in exile and are invited to The Chronicon."
warlock_2="Today’s Warlocks are still practicing Shadow magic, but have expanded their practice to include several other schools of magic, such as Fire, Frost, and Poison. While their focus remains largely on the more destructive and dominating aspects of such magic, they are now more accepted, even though they always remain in suspicion."
warlock_3="While not officially a Warlock, the mad Doctor and his vile experiments did influence their exile. With other tragic events involving Shadow magic, such as The Fallen Temple and The Elven War, the people of the world became keenly aware of the risks, and chose to ban it. However, when the drums of war sounded once again, and armies rallied at The Gates of Hell, the Warlocks answered the call. And this would never be forgotten."
actdesert_0="The Perilous Wastes"
actdesert_1="In the barren lands and endless deserts of the far east, Orcs and Goblins stake their claim. Led by Bone Shamans, masters of life and death, the Orcs are scattered across many settlements, in a constant battle with their surroundings for survival. Among them live the Goblins, who are less organized but more numerous. While capable fighters and magicians on their own, Goblins are often allied with nearby Orc settlements for trade and protection from the many dangers that stalk the barren lands."
actdesert_2="Among the Orcs and Goblins, several historical characters exist, in particular there is a Bone Shaman and a Goblin Tinkerer. While mysteriously unnamed, the duo were involved with the construction of The Chronicon. In fact, the whole idea of The Chronicon is credited to the Goblin Tinkerer, who is a direct ancestor of its current caretaker. However, they both returned to their homelands to guide their people, and their exact fate remains unknown."
actdesert_3="In their lands, many ruins of an ancient civilization exist. Neither Goblin nor Orc have any knowledge of what exactly that civilization was, nor what wiped them out. The ruins are teeming with dark magics, and overrun by undead and other terrible creatures. As such, the ruins sit mostly undisturbed, as Orcs and Goblins alike know better than to enter. Humans however, don’t share the same level of sense."
jones_0="Jones"
jones_1="Even though she's a famous explorer and historian, whose exploits have aided The Chronicon greatly, very little is actually known about Diana Jones. She has been sighted during many historical events, even those many decades apart, which brings many questions and much suspicion about her."
jones_2="Her discoveries about an ancient and wiped out civilization have stirred many questions about our own civilizations and their origins, as our recorded history only goes back a few hundred years. Considering the power of The Chronicon, this raises even more questions among historians. And she has made it her mission to answer them."
beserker_0="The Dragon Tribes"
beserker_1="Long ago, Dragons were a common sight across the lands. There existed several Dragon Tribes that followed and served the great Dragons, and in turn were granted great powers to fulfill their roles. They were the Guardians, who guarded the ancient Dragon Temples which acted as hatcheries. The Frostborn, who lived among the Frost Drakes in the cold mountains of the north to calm their rage. The Skylords who rode the great winged Thunder Dragons far into the skies. And the Dragonkin, a Dragon-Human halfbreed that lived among the wingless Fire Dragons in the barren lands."
beserker_2="During the events that led to the construction of The Chronicon, the Dragons took to the skies and vanished. Without a trace, and without a word to their Tribes. This sent the Tribes into complete disarray, as they felt abandoned and betrayed by their masters. During this time, notable heroes arose to lead their Tribes, to find their old masters, and to discover the cause of their abandonment. One such hero was Balgar the Cunning."
beserker_3="Balgar traveled to the mysterious Caldera, and was ultimately one of the founding members of The Chronicon, and the main reason why the remnants of the Dragon Tribes are welcomed. Today, we simply know them as Beserkers, united in a singular Tribe, welcoming Skylords, Dragonkin, Frostborn, and Guardians alike. Generations later, many now retain powers from several Tribes, and they all still await their old masters. But not to serve them."
acthell_0="The Final Frontier"
acthell_1="While the true enemy was discovered soon after the events of The Elven War, it took far much longer to discover their realm, and amass armies to assault it. Nearly a whole generation had passed since the end of The Elven War and the Gates of Hell were breached. This had allowed the Elves to rebuild, and strong alliances to form between the peoples of the world. But it also allowed the Demons to prepare. And prepared they were."
acthell_2="The Breaching of the Gate was a monumental task which required co-operation between people as never before seen. Humans, Elves, Orcs, and Goblins all fought together to carve a path right up to the gate. Heavily reinforced and protected by foul magics, the gate was at first impenetrable. However by working together, the armies secured and utilized a massive stockpile of demonic explosives, and blasted their way through. On the other side of the gate, a large camp was set up, and reinforcements poured in. Notably, this camp was the first ever settlement built by all members of the alliance."
acthell_3="Together they pushed deeper into the Hellscape, fighting many horrors and aberrations on their way. After a long and terrible campaign, an elite squad of champions reached the very depths, and came upon the plotting mastermind. A great and fearsome beast, partially submerged by the molten rock, summoned hordes of demons and rained fire upon them. Yet they stood victorious, slaying The Beast Below, scattering the remaining demons instantly. The enemy was defeated, and peace would reign for generations."
heroeshell_0="Heroes of Hell"
heroeshell_1="Notable leaders on The Final Frontier were General Jensen, Elder Druid Far’El’Sun, War Shaman Broguk, and Masta Wizza Shizzam. They all led their respective peoples' forces, and worked together admirably, receiving many accolades of war and being hailed as some of the greatest heroes of our time."
heroeshell_2="Many other names would also go into history, rightfully celebrated as heroes. Among them are Major Aulfere, who witnessed unspeakable horrors only to come back stronger and with invaluable information. Master Scout Al’vin, whose finesse and cleverness helped find and secure the explosives needed to breach the gate. And last but not least, the self-proclaimed Demon Hunter brothers, who joined the war effort without being called, and stepped through the gates of Hell to do their part."
heroeshell_3="Of course, among our celebrated heroes, there are also those who never made it back. Those who gave their lives for the safety of their comrades, Human, Elf, Orc, and Goblin alike. They are who we honor most, and their memories are forever contained within The Chronicon. The greatest honor anyone could ever have."
prologue_0="Prologue"
prologue_1="Several generations ago, a great Mausoleum was constructed into the side of a great mountain. Here, Heroes of Old were buried and honored. The Mausoleum was a symbol of peace and unity, as Elves, Humans, and many others were buried here together."
prologue_2="One fateful night, something plummeted from the skies, and struck the mountain. The mountain erupted in violent fire, cracked open, and collapsed in on itself. A Caldera was formed, and in it, strange things began to appear."
prologue_3="This drew the attention of adventures, explorers, and champions of all walks of life. They delved deep into the Caldera, forever imparting their names in history. The strange visions emanating from the Caldera were quickly discovered to be various historical figures and events, all scrambled together in an unstable concoction of memory and fiction. "
prologue_4="It was all linked to the Mausoleum in the mountainside. The memories of the long dead heroes were seeping back into reality, through means no one at the time understood. What was found at the depths of the Caldera the delvers took with them to their graves, but not before working together on a way to preserve these scattered memories."
prologue_5="The Chronicon would come to be constructed over the Caldera itself, feeding on the energies from the depths, and stabilizing the memories into accurate historical simulations. Today, history is remembered, honored, and celebrated by each year sending selected champions into the simulations, to re-live the memories of our fallen heroes."
tinkasdomain_0="Tinka's Domain"
tinkasdomain_1="Tinka comes from a long line of Goblin Tinkerers, one of which was part of the construction of the Chronicon itself. He alone knows how to operate and maintain its inner workings, and as such has been able to craft a dimension for himself."
tinkasdomain_2="In a pocket of unsimulated space, Tinka has built his own domain, where he is acting as king, and he taps into the less stable memories. Initially an unsanctioned and rogue project, it is now accepted by members of the Chronicon as a necessary function. "
tinkasdomain_3="The unstable memories that the strongest and most experienced heroes may delve into still produce the memory crystals and essences needed to further build stable memories. In fact, they produce larger amounts than the stable memories do, so it has been an efficient way to restore additional historical events to the Chronicon."
tinkasdomain_4="As such, Tinka’s Domain is now an official part of The Chronicon, and all services rendered in The Chronicon are also available in Tinka’s Domain. Tinka still sits on a throne and pretends to be a king, however some may say he has earned it."
bramley_0="Bramley"
bramley_1="Bramley is a curious fellow who explores the world, and beyond. In his travels through time and space he has come across Tinka’s Domain, and forged a friendship with the Goblin. Not much is known about his origins, but he is wise beyond his years, and knows a lot more than he lets on."
bramley_2="With the help of The Chronicon and the unstable energies of Tinka’s Domain, Bramley has set up an Expedition plan to delve back in time to secure and safeguard the Ancient Beasts. These beasts are origin creatures of our world, and existed long before Humans, Elves, or any other intelligent life. Why exactly Bramley wants to preserve them and revive them only he knows, but he does have ulterior motives."
mechanist_0="The Mechanists' Guild"
mechanist_1="The Mechanists originally rose from within The Templar Orders, as specialists in weapon and armor manufacture and maintenance. As the technologies of the world quickly advanced, in no small part due to the construction of The Chronicon, so did the roles of The Mechanists. Their equipment became increasingly advanced and complicated, and increasingly specialized. Who better to wear it than themselves?"
mechanist_2="As such The Mechanists became their own Order, and eventually separated from the Knights Templars entirely, as the definitions and specializations of the orders tightened. The Mechanists were still trained within several schools of magic, which they combined with their superior mechanical knowledge. Much of their technology is very similar to the inner workings of The Chronicon, and as such they were involved during its construction. Eventually, they would come to create machines that were fueled by magic, known as the Mana-Mechano."
mechanist_3="Where the knowledge from all these things come from is heavily disputed. The Mechanists claim it was from their own hard work, of course, but the rate of which technology advanced has made many suspicious of their claims. As powerful and advanced as their technology is, it is rarely used outside of The Mechanists’ Guild - partly due to the suspicions and distrusts, and partly because they want to keep control over it. Imagine what it could do in the wrong hands..."